meta:
  origin:
    # Data product / Snapshot
    title: Historical mortality tables, 1900–1998 (HIST290 and HIST290A)
    description: |-
      These tables from the National Center for Health Statistics (NCHS) give the number of deaths and death rates in the United States for a fixed list of causes, every year from 1900 to 1998, by sex, race, and 10-year age group. Death rates are deaths per 100,000 people in each group.

      Before 1933, the figures cover only the “death-registration states”: the states that recorded deaths reliably enough to be included. These grew from ten states and the District of Columbia in 1900 to the whole country in 1933.

      Causes of death are classified with the International Classification of Diseases (ICD), which was revised several times over the century. NCHS publishes one table per revision period, and the list of causes grows from 16 in 1900–1939 to 72 in 1979–1998. The names and definitions of some causes change between periods, so a cause’s trend can jump when a new revision comes into use.
    # NOTE: The tables were produced between the 1970s and 2000. This is the "last reviewed" date of the NCHS page
    # that links them (the files' own timestamps date from a 2024 website migration).
    date_published: "2015-11-06"

    # Citation
    producer: National Center for Health Statistics
    citation_full: |-
      National Center for Health Statistics. Historical Data, 1900–1998: HIST290, Death rates for selected causes by 10-year age groups, race, and sex: Death registration states, 1900–32, and United States, 1933–98; and HIST290A, Deaths for selected causes by 10-year age groups, race, and sex: Death registration states, 1900–32, and United States, 1933–98. Hyattsville, MD: National Center for Health Statistics.
    attribution_short: NCHS

    # Files
    url_main: https://www.cdc.gov/nchs/nvss/mortality_historical_data.htm
    date_accessed: 2026-11-12

    # License
    license:
      name: Public domain
      url: https://www.cdc.gov/other/agencymaterials.html
